{
  "case_id": "2009-08-1498",
  "document_hash": "3ad62dc4846c552344a5f448fce4bd723e7c72509cac6ba04faf6667fda1cb68",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ad62dc4846c552344a5f448fce4bd723e7c72509cac6ba04faf6667fda1cb68",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ad62dc4846c-0000-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It is undisputed that the Kurdistan Workers Party engages in a wide range of lawful activities and that plaintiffs seek to support only lawful ends."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ad62dc4846c552344a5f448fce4bd723e7c72509cac6ba04faf6667fda1cb68",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ad62dc4846c-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: But, Mr. Cole, don't you agree that some of the speech could be regulated?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Humanitarian Law Project",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ad62dc4846c552344a5f448fce4bd723e7c72509cac6ba04faf6667fda1cb68",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ad62dc4846c-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It\u2019s core -- and I think the reason, Your Honor, is it is core political speech on issues of public concern. It is advocating only lawful, peaceable activities. This Court has never upheld the criminal prohibition of lawful speech on issues of public concern."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ad62dc4846c552344a5f448fce4bd723e7c72509cac6ba04faf6667fda1cb68",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ad62dc4846c-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Well, could the government, I assume -- I assume you will say \"yes\" -- could the government forbid any NGO or other organization or person from giving tsunami aid to one of these organizations, from giving them money?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Attorney General",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ad62dc4846c552344a5f448fce4bd723e7c72509cac6ba04faf6667fda1cb68",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ad62dc4846c-0000-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It hasn't criminalized speech. It has criminalized providing aid and assistance to these organizations. Most of that aid and assistance that is prohibited is not in the form of speech, but it happens to include speech as well."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ad62dc4846c552344a5f448fce4bd723e7c72509cac6ba04faf6667fda1cb68",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ad62dc4846c-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why isn't that a sufficiently serious reason for the government to do what it's done here?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Kagan",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ad62dc4846c552344a5f448fce4bd723e7c72509cac6ba04faf6667fda1cb68",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ad62dc4846c-0001-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress was the reasonable person here. And Congress reasonably decided that when you help a terrorist -- foreign terrorist organization's legal activities, you\u2019re also helping the foreign terrorist organization's illegal activities."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ad62dc4846c552344a5f448fce4bd723e7c72509cac6ba04faf6667fda1cb68",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ad62dc4846c-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Why do you say Congress clearly did not intend that? You know, I would have guessed that you are providing a service or personnel when you make yourself a member of the organization. Why do you say Congress clearly did not intend it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Kagan",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ad62dc4846c552344a5f448fce4bd723e7c72509cac6ba04faf6667fda1cb68",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ad62dc4846c-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL KAGAN: Yes, I think that would be a service. In other words, not an amicus brief just to make sure that we understand each other. The Petitioners can file amicus briefs in a case that might involve the PKK or the LTTE for themselves, but to the extent that a lawyer drafts an amicus brief for the PKK or for the LTTE, that that's the amicus party, then that indeed would be prohibited. That's the kind of service that --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ad62dc4846c552344a5f448fce4bd723e7c72509cac6ba04faf6667fda1cb68",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ad62dc4846c-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Do you stick with the argument made below that it's unlawful to file an amicus brief?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Kagan",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ad62dc4846c552344a5f448fce4bd723e7c72509cac6ba04faf6667fda1cb68",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ad62dc4846c-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL KAGAN: The discussion must stop when you -- when you go over the line into giving valuable advice, training, support to these organizations. At that point --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ad62dc4846c552344a5f448fce4bd723e7c72509cac6ba04faf6667fda1cb68",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ad62dc4846c-0002-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL KAGAN: Again, the government did not bring this action. Judge Fertig and the Petitioners brought this action to try to get a declaratory judgment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Humanitarian Law Project",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ad62dc4846c552344a5f448fce4bd723e7c72509cac6ba04faf6667fda1cb68",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ad62dc4846c-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The government has spent a decade arguing that our clients cannot advocate for peace, cannot inform about international human rights."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Humanitarian Law Project",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ad62dc4846c552344a5f448fce4bd723e7c72509cac6ba04faf6667fda1cb68",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ad62dc4846c-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We\u2019ve been doing this kind of lawful activity. We think it's our right, but we\u2019re not going to risk going to jail for 15 years to do it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ad62dc4846c552344a5f448fce4bd723e7c72509cac6ba04faf6667fda1cb68",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ad62dc4846c-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If O'Brien applies, what remains of your case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ad62dc4846c552344a5f448fce4bd723e7c72509cac6ba04faf6667fda1cb68",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ad62dc4846c-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That analysis of the activities that you are proposing has not been done by the lower courts, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Humanitarian Law Project",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ad62dc4846c552344a5f448fce4bd723e7c72509cac6ba04faf6667fda1cb68",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ad62dc4846c-0003-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think it would be appropriate to remand for -- for application of strict scrutiny if you read it that O'Brien doesn't apply."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Humanitarian Law Project",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ad62dc4846c552344a5f448fce4bd723e7c72509cac6ba04faf6667fda1cb68",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ad62dc4846c-0003-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We\u2019re seeking to teach them how to advocate for lawful human rights or --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Humanitarian Law Project",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1498",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3ad62dc4846c552344a5f448fce4bd723e7c72509cac6ba04faf6667fda1cb68",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3ad62dc4846c-0003-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And we have suggested that you should, therefore, interpret the statute in -- consistent with that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1498",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "3ad62dc4846c552344a5f448fce4bd723e7c72509cac6ba04faf6667fda1cb68",
